WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:04.850
Petyr Baelish: Prince Maegor, a warrior who
was proud and arrogant.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:10.680
Maegor agreed to marry the High Septon's niece
to unite the Faith and the Crown, but then

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:17.269
secretly wed a second wife in a Valyrian ceremony
artfully combining bigamy and heresy.

00:00:17.269 --> 00:00:21.519
When word of it got out, the King was forced
to exile Maegor and choose a septon as his

00:00:21.519 --> 00:00:23.079
new Hand.

00:00:23.079 --> 00:00:25.119
But the damage had been done.

00:00:25.119 --> 00:00:29.789
The King had trusted in family, and his brother
had set off a rebellion that would claim his

00:00:29.789 --> 00:00:32.399
rule and his life.

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:37.230
The High Sparrow: When Aegon's heir wed his
daughter to his son, the Faith could brook

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:39.920
such abomination no longer.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:43.750
The High Septon led the denunciation of the
Targaryens.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:48.510
And all over Westeros, the Faith Militant
took up their swords against the dynasty and

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:49.690
its supporters.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:55.499
The Faith Militant set upon and punished the
septon who had performed the ceremony.

00:00:55.499 --> 00:01:02.350
A few of the Faith Militant's more militant
members even scaled the walls of the castle

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:07.740
and would have slain the king and his family,
had a knight of the Kingsguard not intervened.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:14.150
Frightened, the king fled to Dragonstone,
where he soon died of cramps.

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:19.140
And so ascended the king's younger brother,
Maegor the Cruel.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:24.700
His first act was to challenge the Faith Militant
to kill him if they believed his rule to be

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:26.110
ungodly.

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:30.100
To the order's eternal credit, they accepted.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:38.200
Ser Damon Morrigen proposed a "Trial by Seven,"
Ser Damon and six of the Faith Militant against

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.060
the king and his six champions.

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:47.330
It was a contest in which the kingdom itself
was at stake, and the accounts and tales are

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:48.330
many.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:55.640
But at the end of it, Maegor alone lived,
proving that the throne was rightfully his.

00:01:55.640 --> 00:02:01.600
He mounted the black dragon, Balerion, and
burned down the sept in King's Landing while

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:05.240
the Faith Militant were inside at morning
prayers.

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:11.660
The screams of the burning and dying men were
said to echo throughout the city.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:16.920
Though Maegor had won the trial by seven,
he demanded the complete destruction of the

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:20.350
Faith Militant and the Faith itself, if necessary.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:23.910
He made war upon the order wherever he found
it.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:30.270
Yet the Faith Militant would not surrender,
raising armies of their own and turning Maegor's

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:32.260
own lords against him.

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:38.550
The Father's justice may not always be swift,
but it is certain.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:42.640
One morning, Maegor was found dead on the
Iron Throne.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:43.890
No one knows how.

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:49.760
Viserys Targaryen: After the Conquest, when
men looked up, they saw dragons.

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:55.700
Nobles learned to keep their eyes down, but
the gods weren't used to sharing the heavens.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:03:01.070
When Aegon died, the High Septon led the Faith
and its army in revolt, claiming that the

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:06.250
Valyrian tradition of wedding brother to sister
was an abomination in the eyes of the Seven.

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:11.410
Though no one could explain where the divine
Mother and Father had come from.

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:18.180
My ancestor Maegor the Wise, or Maegor the
Cruel as men slander him, put a bounty on

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:24.990
the head of every militant priest, and miraculously
the Faith soon returned to the septs.

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:30.650
Varys: Though the Targaryens had forged the
Seven Kingdoms in fire and blood, they didn't

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:32.650
govern with them.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:34.010
Until they did.

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:41.120
Maegor, First of His Name, defined counsel
as confirmation and disagreement as treason.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:44.620
Three Grand Maesters tried to avert disaster.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:49.130
Instead of taking their advice, Maegor took
their heads.

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:53.819
As a second son and exile, Maegor was never
meant to rule.

00:03:53.819 --> 00:03:58.150
But no sooner did Maegor hear of his brother's
death that he flew Balerion to Dragonstone

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:01.040
and demanded the crown.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.770
Only the Grand Maester dared object that the
throne should pass to his older brother's

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:07.310
firstborn son, Prince Aegon.

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:12.380
Maegor insisted that the Iron Throne should
go to the man with the strength to seize it,

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:15.400
and beheaded the Grand Maester.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:18.530
Prince Aegon soon took him at his word.

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:23.479
He claimed his father's dragon, raised a host
of Westermen, and marched on King's Landing

00:04:23.479 --> 00:04:26.210
while Maegor was in Oldtown.

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:29.990
Far from the capital, Maegor couldn't rally
an army to match Aegon's.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:35.060
So he ordered his banners to swarm Aegon's
larger army from all sides, confusing the

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:37.800
young prince and slowing his advance.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:43.800
Beneath the Gods Eye, Maegor's disparate forces
came together and attacked Aegon as Maegor

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:46.129
himself swooped down from the clouds.

00:04:46.129 --> 00:04:51.229
For the first time since the Doom of Valyria,
dragon fought dragon in the sky.

00:04:51.229 --> 00:04:57.400
But Aegon's dragon was no match for Balerion
the Dread, who was four times its size.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:01.370
When Aegon fell to his death, his army broke
and fled.

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:06.090
For slaying his own nephew, Maegor forever
after became known as "The Cruel."

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:09.610
Though, of course, not to his face.

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:15.749
The next Grand Maester dared object to Maegor
taking a third wife when taking his second

00:05:15.749 --> 00:05:21.090
wife had ruined his brother's reign because
Maegor's first wife was the niece of the High

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:22.090
Septon.

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:26.309
But Maegor beheaded the Grand Maester and
declared war on the Faith.

00:05:26.309 --> 00:05:31.629
He set fire to the Riverlands, the Westerlands,
and the Reach in a campaign to root out disloyal

00:05:31.629 --> 00:05:35.669
lords and sponsored a more pliant High Septon.

00:05:35.669 --> 00:05:37.759
None of it worked.

00:05:37.759 --> 00:05:41.830
Maegor may have returned to the capital with
two thousand skulls of the Faith Militant,

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:43.699
but most of them weren't soldiers.

00:05:43.699 --> 00:05:49.120
They were simple folk who had sheltered the
outlaw septons or turned out in droves to

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:52.009
hear them denounce the wicked king.

00:05:52.009 --> 00:05:57.569
The third Grand Maester dared to declare Maegor
the father of his own heir.

00:05:57.569 --> 00:06:04.040
But when his second wife miscarried, and Maegor
saw the monstrous stillbirth, Maegor beheaded

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:07.580
the Grand Maester for his insolent adherence
to truth.

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:13.650
So he had no one to warn him when his third
wife, sensing an advantage, declared that

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:18.949
his second wife had been unfaithful, and produced
a list of potential fathers of the misshapen

00:06:18.949 --> 00:06:20.460
child.

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:25.419
Not only did Maegor execute his second wife
and her father, his own Hand of the King,

00:06:25.419 --> 00:06:30.280
but he also marched on her family's castle
and slaughtered everyone who bore a drop of

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:32.400
her family's blood.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:36.270
But his third wife couldn't give him a child
either.

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:41.689
Desperate to cement his stolen throne with
an heir, Maegor took three wives at once,

00:06:41.689 --> 00:06:46.779
known as the Black Brides because each were
women he'd widowed in his wars.

00:06:46.779 --> 00:06:53.300
All three women grew full with child in time,
but each gave birth to the same twisted monstrosities

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:55.300
as his second wife.

00:06:55.300 --> 00:07:00.979
One need not be a maester, much less a Grand
Maester, to deduce the common thread here.

00:07:00.979 --> 00:07:06.629
Though Maegor stamped out the fires of rebellion,
his cruelty and fear only scattered more tinder

00:07:06.629 --> 00:07:11.149
over the realm until even the smallest ember
could set the realm alight.

00:07:11.149 --> 00:07:16.809
One day, the Faith Militant emerged from the
shadows, and the lords sent to quash it joined

00:07:16.809 --> 00:07:18.259
it instead.

00:07:18.259 --> 00:07:21.529
His Hand resigned and retired to his island
home.

00:07:21.529 --> 00:07:26.770
Finally, House Baratheon declared for Maegor's
own nephew as the rightful king.

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:32.800
The Lannisters, Tyrells, and Arryns soon joined,
adding more than half the might of Westeros

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:35.559
to the prince and his two dragons.

00:07:35.559 --> 00:07:41.289
Which became three when Maegor's niece and
involuntary Black Bride stole away from the

00:07:41.289 --> 00:07:42.970
Red Keep with her dragon.

00:07:42.970 --> 00:07:45.449
Her treason wasn't even the last.

00:07:45.449 --> 00:07:49.529
Maegor's own lord admiral sailed the Royal
Fleet into his nephew's harbor.

00:07:49.529 --> 00:07:55.279
But most fitting of all, when Maegor tried
to send ravens to call his banners, he found

00:07:55.279 --> 00:08:01.629
that his fourth Grand Maester had learned
from his predecessors and fled.

00:08:01.629 --> 00:08:05.020
Maegor spent one final night on the Iron Throne.

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:11.110
He was found in the morning with his wrists
slashed and one of the throne's blades jutting

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:12.869
from his throat.

00:08:12.869 --> 00:08:18.050
Nobody knows if it was one of his queens or
Kingsguard or one of the thousands who wanted

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:19.050
him dead.

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:24.229
Or even Maegor himself, frustrated that his
body had failed his will.

00:08:24.229 --> 00:08:28.599
Whoever the culprit, no doubt he died as all
tyrants do.

00:08:28.599 --> 00:08:31.059
Believing that history would vindicate him.

00:08:31.059 --> 00:08:33.060
It hasn't.

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:37.510
History may be written with fire and blood,
but histories aren't.

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:41.229
As any good advisor could have warned him.

00:08:41.229 --> 00:08:46.490
Joffrey Baratheon: When the builders finally
finished the Red Keep, Maegor executed them

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:49.800
all to keep its secrets safe.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:57.269
Rumor has it, miles of hidden passageways
run behind the walls and under the floors.

00:08:57.269 --> 00:08:59.529
One day I'll have to find them.

00:08:59.529 --> 00:09:02.029
Traitors and women work in shadows.

00:09:02.029 --> 00:09:06.120
A king has no need for secrecy.

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:12.399
Now, people name Maegor "the Cruel," but I
doubt any dared in his day.

00:09:12.399 --> 00:09:17.460
His strength was all too rare in the degenerate
Targaryen blood.

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:23.800
Varys: And Maegor decided to replace a monument
to the gods with a monument to his family:

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:25.089
the Dragonpit.

00:09:25.089 --> 00:09:31.950
Qyburn: Labor proved elusive, however, for
after the Red Keep was finished, Maegor had

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:37.170
hosted a three-day feast for all builders,
stonemasons, and carpenters who had worked

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:38.509
to build it.

00:09:38.509 --> 00:09:44.709
At its conclusion, he slaughtered them, so
that only he would know the castle's secrets.

00:09:44.709 --> 00:09:49.949
So many men fled the construction of the Dragonpit
that Maegor was forced to employ the prisoners

00:09:49.949 --> 00:09:55.760
of the city dungeons, supplemented by skilled
and ignorant builders from across the Narrow

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:56.760
Sea.

00:09:56.760 --> 00:10:02.520
Varys: Aegon's own son, Maegor the Cruel,
was killed by the very Iron Throne his father

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:05.790
had forged if you believe the tales.

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:14.899
If you don't, then perhaps "the Cruel" is
not a wise name for a king to earn.

